$ gragas history --help
--- stdout

  Every change to a rule's life, one row
  each, in the order
  the history keeps: its number, what
  was done, to which rule,
  by whom, when, the plan that was
  accepted and the decision
  taken. Give a rule's id, or an id it
  had before it was
  renumbered, to list only that rule's
  rows.

  A line that cannot be read is skipped
  and counted, and a
  link that does not hold is listed
  under the rows. It reads
  and changes nothing.

    gragas history
    gragas history <id>
    gragas history --at v1.2.0
    gragas history --json

  USAGE


    gragas history [id] [--flags]


  FLAGS

    --accessible  Plain questions
                  (ACCESSIBLE)
    --at          Read the history as it
                  is at this tag, commit
                  or branch
    --config      The settings file
                  (GRAGAS_CONFIG)
    --entity      List only the rows
                  about this entity, as
                  the history names it
    -h --help     Help for history
    --json        Answer in one JSON
                  document
    --no-color    No colour (NO_COLOR)
    --plain       Print plainly: nothing
                  moves

--- stderr
